cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite this repository."
type: software
title: "Laminar: Infrastructure for laminar stacking (default: honeycomb symmetry, JAM notation)"
abstract: >
  Laminar is a Rust workspace for generating, canonicalizing, classifying,
  and sampling stacking configurations of layered materials. The default
  (and only) instantiation in v0.1 targets honeycomb layers
  (G = S3 x Z/2) with JAM notation; the architecture supports additional
  symmetry modules and notations via the StackingMode trait. Features:
  O(k) canonicalization (Theorem 3 of *Orbits as Multisets*), canonical
  augmentation (Theorem 2 of *Growing as Pruning*), word-based cell
  classification (PP/Pp/pP/Ap, *Stacking as Words*), CLI (sandwich,
  compare, modules), Python bindings (PyO3), and CIF export.
authors:
